Subject: [PATCH] platform/surface: scope the SAM suspend workaround to SP12

The reference surface/0006 disables D3 handle closing for every OF Surface
device. Restrict that workaround to the Surface Pro 12in root compatible;
retain the upstream default on all other machines and the ACPI path.
This preserves the reference SP12 behavior pending hardware validation.
Authorship and DCO provenance are unresolved in the vendor input.

diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/aggregator/controller.c b/drivers/platform/surface/aggregator/controller.c
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/aggregator/controller.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/aggregator/controller.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <linux/list.h>
 #include <linux/lockdep.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/rculist.h>
 #include <linux/rbtree.h>
 #include <linux/rwsem.h>
@@ -1156,6 +1157,11 @@
 	 * identical values, which makes them good defaults.
 	 */
 	caps->d3_closes_handle = true;
+
+	/* Keep the SAM handle open across suspend on Surface Pro 12in. */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,surface-pro-12in"))
+		caps->d3_closes_handle = false;
+
 	caps->screen_on_sleep_idle_timeout = 5000;
 	caps->screen_off_sleep_idle_timeout = 30;
 	caps->ssh_buffer_size = 48;
